--- !u!114 &6380971797498219356
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2179195205541631995}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b><size=+10>How To Play</size></b>

    Select any exposed card from
    the bottom of a Tableau column that is either one rank higher or one rank lower
    than the top card of the Foundation pile (regardless of suit). For example, if
    a 7 is on the Foundation, you can play an 8 or a 6 onto it.


    In traditional
    rules, Kings are the highest rank and stop a sequence (no card can be played
    on a King), while Aces are lowest. In most variants, Queens can be played on
    Kings, and in the Putt Putt variant, Kings can wrap to Aces and vice versa. When
    you run out of valid moves in the Tableau, tap the Stock to deal a new card onto
    the Foundation to continue your sequence.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7953b3aff3010de47827554b597de01f, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6622473957194473056, guid: 7953b3aff3010de47827554b597de01f, type: 2}
